## The 6-Row Heuristics Audit Table

Before completing any implementation plan or edit, answer all 6 rows in the proposal or changelog. Any "No" on requirements 1–5 or "Yes" on 6 means **redesign**:

| # | Question | Pass Requirement |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Single owner? | **Yes** — one system/API owns this behavior end-to-end; no parallel owner |
| 2 | One apply path? | **Yes** — no second preview/save/commit/hover path |
| 3 | No identity branches? | **Yes** — no `if node/tab/scene/skill_id ==` for this behavior |
| 4 | No UI-only state? | **Yes** — sim/commit/slots/`GameSettings` see the identical truth |
| 5 | Reusable? | **Yes** — other skills/screens use the same path without new `if` branches |
| 6 | Obsolete path removed? | **Yes** — deleted old hack/obsolete path in the **same** change |

**Changelog Requirement:** Always state **How this protects SSOT**, **Heuristics added:** (`none` or list), and **Why (not) heuristic:**. Vacuous lines count as missing.

